{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"group-perfho","type":"group","x":1260,"y":40,"width":3039,"height":5720,"label":"Perf Hotspots"},
		{"id":"group-perffu90b","type":"group","x":640,"y":40,"width":540,"height":4280,"label":"Perf Fused Loop"},
		{"id":"group-perfba","type":"group","x":20,"y":40,"width":540,"height":1820,"label":"Perf Baseline"},
		{"id":"group-perfgu","type":"group","x":2860,"y":820,"width":540,"height":1040,"label":"Perf Guardrails"},
		{"id":"group-perfre","type":"group","x":3480,"y":820,"width":540,"height":1040,"label":"Perf Reporting"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"## Legend\n🔴 **Red** = To Do (ready)\n⬜ **Gray** = Blocked\n🟠 **Orange** = Doing\n🔵 **Cyan** = Ready to review\n🟢 **Green** = Done\n🟣 **Purple** = Proposed by agent","x":-540,"y":-310,"width":380,"height":230,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"canvas-warnings","type":"text","text":"## Warnings\n✓ None","x":-540,"y":-530,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"canvas-errors","type":"text","text":"## Errors\n✓ None","x":-540,"y":-750,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"3cbdcc10","type":"text","text":"## PB-01 Freeze representative realtime benchmark\nFrozen the conservative benchmark contract in docs/performance_realtime_baseline.md using scripts/profile_simulation.py with 0.2 mm and 0.05 mm meshes, steps=200000, warmup=5000, repeats=2, hotspots=both, and baseline report outputs/profiling/realtime_baseline_20260321.json. Current medians are 37714.66 steps/s at 0.2 mm (26.51x slower than realtime) and 24372.43 steps/s at 0.05 mm (41.03x slower than realtime). Dashboard artifact: outputs/profiling/performance_dashboard.html.","x":80,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"d378c8c0","type":"text","text":"## PB-02 Stabilize benchmark conditions\nAdded machine and power-context capture to scripts/profile_simulation.py so each profiling report records host/platform, power source, battery state, active power scheme, processor policy caps, frequency/performance counters, and a comparability assessment. Added the repeatable preset runner scripts/profile_realtime_baseline.py to run the frozen conservative baseline and refresh the HTML dashboard in one command. Updated the dashboard meta panel to surface power context and comparability notes. Verified with pytest tests/test_profile_baseline_preset.py tests/test_perf_dashboard.py -q and a real baseline run to outputs/profiling/realtime_baseline_pb02_verify.json. Fresh baseline medians: 40516.49 steps/s at 0.2 mm and 31411.69 steps/s at 0.05 mm; current run was on AC, Balanced plan, max processor state 100, with no battery or policy-cap warning recorded.","x":80,"y":860,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c76f8859","type":"text","text":"## PG-01 Define no-regression fidelity checks\nDefined explicit fidelity guardrails in scripts/profile_simulation.py by adding per-scenario fidelity_signature data and optional baseline comparison via --compare-to. Guardrails now cover termination_reason, crater_count, crater_volume_mm3, mean wire temperature, max wire damage, final workpiece position, and dashboard-required signals (wire_temperature, wire_material_positions_mm, wire_head_idx, wire_offset_mm). Regenerated the canonical baseline at outputs/profiling/realtime_baseline_20260322_i1.json so it includes fidelity_signature, updated docs/README with the comparison workflow, and added regression tests in tests/test_profile_fidelity.py. Verified with pytest tests/test_profile_fidelity.py tests/test_profile_baseline_preset.py tests/test_perf_dashboard.py -q (8 passed) and a self-compare of the canonical baseline report.","x":2920,"y":860,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"e5f903cc","type":"text","text":"## PB-04 Lower conservative benchmark current to I1\nChange the conservative realtime baseline preset from I5 to I1 so the benchmark avoids wire-broken termination when possible, then regenerate the baseline JSON, docs, and dashboard against the new contract.","x":80,"y":1640,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"f34bd19e","type":"text","text":"## PG-02 Automate perf-vs-fidelity verification\nMake it easy to rerun throughput and fidelity checks together before accepting optimizations.","x":2920,"y":1640,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"803d9f8e","type":"text","text":"## PR-01 Build bottleneck dashboard HTML\nExpanded the performance dashboard in scripts/build_perf_dashboard.py from a static summary into an interactive report. Added a plot control bar with metric selection plus manual y-axis min/max inputs and apply/reset actions, and replaced the flat hotspot section with a module drilldown panel that lets you click a module such as wire and inspect the heaviest matching cProfile functions/lines per scenario. Regenerated outputs/profiling/performance_dashboard.html and tightened tests/test_perf_dashboard.py so the smoke test now covers the new plot controls and drilldown section. Verified with python scripts/build_perf_dashboard.py and pytest tests/test_perf_dashboard.py -q (1 passed).","x":3540,"y":860,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"91bfd94b","type":"text","text":"## PR-02 Track progress history\nExtended the standalone performance dashboard to track archived progress instead of only raw snapshots. scripts/build_perf_dashboard.py now reads verification_summary from candidate reports, computes per-scenario deltas versus the previous archived run and versus the baseline, adds a Before / After panel for the latest verified candidate, and shows Vs previous / Vs baseline columns in both the latest snapshot table and the full history table. Regenerated outputs/profiling/performance_dashboard.html from 10 archived profiling reports, including outputs/profiling/perf_candidate_pg02_pr02_verify.json, and updated README.md plus docs/performance_realtime_baseline.md so the verification-and-history workflow is documented. Verified with pytest tests/test_perf_verification_workflow.py tests/test_perf_dashboard.py tests/test_profile_baseline_preset.py tests/test_profile_fidelity.py -q (10 passed).","x":3540,"y":1640,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"8fb27d7c","type":"text","text":"## PH-11 Compile ignition discharge state machine\nMove the ignition hot path into a compiled helper covering idle, open, spark, and short transitions, timers, and scalar state updates. Preserve existing ignition behavior and fidelity signatures.","x":1320,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"498c0926","type":"text","text":"## PH-12 Replace ignition mode branching with lookup tables\nFlattened ignition current-mode handling into a crater-backed lookup table and added a cached generator-settings resolver so update() no longer redoes mode/default branching every microstep. Added regression coverage in tests/test_env_integration.py. Isolated same-session microbenchmark on the local src tree showed the new resolver 3.36x faster than the old getter chain for 1M iterations. outputs/profiling/perf_candidate_ph12_verify.json passed fidelity and pytest -q passed (79 passed), but the end-to-end wall-clock comparison versus PH-11 was not clean because the whole run was slower under a different machine state while module shares stayed roughly flat.","x":1320,"y":860,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"668485d3","type":"text","text":"## PH-14 Compile dielectric microstep kernel\nCompile the dielectric hot path and cache invariant coefficients so debris, cavity, flow, and temperature updates stop paying Python overhead every microstep.","x":1810,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"1ee010bb","type":"text","text":"## PH-15 Fuse mechanics update with termination checks\nReduce microstep Python overhead by tightening mechanics update, target-distance checks, and scalar termination bookkeeping into a fast path without changing state semantics.","x":2300,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"125f56aa","type":"text","text":"## PH-16 Whole-env compiled inner loop with modular fallback\nAdd an optional compiled microstep loop that advances the standard modules through shared state while keeping the current modular Python path as a fallback for compatibility and experimentation. Keep module-level reset and logging contracts intact.","x":1320,"y":5540,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"f9d70be6","type":"text","text":"## PH-02 Reduce ignition short-circuit overhead\nSpecialized ignition short-circuit detection for the common benchmark path: active short timers now count down in Python, new-short rolls use one batched RNG call to preserve sequence with less overhead, and the no-random-shorts path uses a simpler compiled debris-only helper. Added low-level regression coverage in tests/test_ignition_kernels.py and full-suite verification. outputs/profiling/perf_candidate_ph02_verify.json passed fidelity; versus perf_candidate_ph12_verify.json throughput improved +25.75 at 0.05 mm / 1600 seg, with ignition wall share dropping 23.95 and 21.02. Same-session 1M-step A/B on 0.05 mm / 1600 seg: 14.26 s old vs 13.14 s new (+8.53).","x":1320,"y":1640,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"21775b2a","type":"text","text":"## PH-03 Reduce environment bookkeeping overhead \nAdded a base-env step fast path that inlines default action intake, termination checks, and default obs/reward handling while preserving subclass overrides. Same-session 1M-step A/B improved 0.20 mm from 91361 to 99572 steps/s (+9.0) with identical final state. Standard verification versus the PH-17 candidate improved 0.20 mm from 80192 to 92275 steps/s (+15.1), with fidelity passing.","x":1320,"y":2420,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a1478aa8","type":"text","text":"## PH-05 Eliminate O(N) wire rollover copies\n Implemented an equivalent offset-based transport model in src/wedm/modules/wire.py: wire positions now advance through a scalar offset over a fixed position template, and temperature/damage are only shifted when a fresh segment actually rolls in. State export still emits physical-order wire positions for logging and dashboard consumers, reset now re-syncs mirrored wire position signals, and tests/test_env_integration.py adds a forced-rollover regression. Verified in outputs/profiling/perf_candidate_ph05_verify.json: fidelity PASS; wire transport share dropped from 6.07 on 0.20 mm and from 5.66 on 0.05 mm vs perf_candidate_ph04_verify.json, with median throughput improving +29.57 respectively.","x":1320,"y":3200,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"e2af75aa","type":"text","text":"## PH-06 Reduce wire state-sync and export copy cost\n Updated src/wedm/modules/wire.py so EDMState aliases the live wire buffers instead of receiving fresh temperature, damage, and position copies every step. Reset now binds state.wire_temperature/state.wire_damage/state.wire_material_positions_mm directly to the internal arrays, and _sync_state_views only refreshes the position buffer when needed and rebinds state back to the live buffers if something replaced them. Added tests/test_env_integration.py coverage for live-buffer aliasing and verified logger compatibility with the existing logger export tests. Verified in outputs/profiling/perf_candidate_ph06_verify.json: fidelity PASS; state_sync share dropped from 8.64 on 0.20 mm and from 9.99 on 0.05 mm vs perf_candidate_ph05_verify.json, with median throughput improving +0.55 respectively.","x":1810,"y":3200,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"2aa0fa92","type":"text","text":"## PH-07 Reduce wire thermal-core memory traffic\nReworked src/wedm/modules/wire.py so the normal update path and the profiled path both use a fused Numba thermal kernel instead of the old vectorized NumPy slice pipeline. The new kernel applies conduction, convection, Joule heating, plasma heat, and the spool boundary in-place using the existing scratch buffer, and convection loss coefficients are now cached in conv_loss_coeff when flow changes instead of recomputed as h_eff_zone * A every microstep. Added tests/test_wire_kernels.py to compare the fused kernel against a plain NumPy reference, and verified the full suite plus outputs/profiling/perf_candidate_ph07_verify.json. Fidelity PASS; versus perf_candidate_ph06_verify.json, median throughput improved +50.14 on 0.05 mm, while wire thermal_core share dropped from 35.90 and from 40.85 respectively.","x":3819,"y":3200,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"1955ab9e","type":"text","text":"## PH-08 Fuse wire damage into compiled core\nFused wire damage accumulation and max-damage / break detection into the compiled thermal kernel, so wire update no longer pays a separate full-array damage pass. Added low-level regression coverage in tests/test_wire_kernels.py against the legacy thermal-plus-damage composition. outputs/profiling/perf_candidate_ph08_verify.json passed fidelity; versus perf_candidate_ph02_verify.json throughput improved +2.56 at 0.05 mm / 1600 seg, with wire wall share dropping 38.14 and 45.26. Same-session 1M-step A/B on 0.05 mm / 1600 seg: 13.60 s old vs 12.63 s new (+7.70). pytest -q passed (82 passed).","x":1320,"y":3980,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"505e33d0","type":"text","text":"## PH-17 Prototype wider compiled wire step\n\nCompiled wire step Added a non-profile fast path that fuses transport rollover, discharge partitioning, and thermal-damage update into one compiled helper while leaving the profiled wire path unchanged for drilldown reporting. Same-session 1M-step A/B versus the pre-PH17 wire path improved 0.20 mm from 102652 to 104235 steps/s (+1.5) with identical final workpiece position and no wire break. Full fidelity verification passed.","x":1810,"y":4760,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"768900ff","type":"text","text":"## PH-10 Optimize hot-segment damage tracking with full export\nPrototyped a hot-index damage path that only updated segments above the temperature threshold while preserving full wire_damage exports, and added a multi-step whole-field regression in tests/test_wire_kernels.py. The isolated same-session 1M-step A/B was mixed: 0.20 mm regressed from 118740 to 106797 steps/s (-10.1%), while 0.05 mm improved from 91708 to 94043 steps/s (+2.5%). Standard verification versus the current PH-13 candidate also regressed coarse throughput (109638 to 101931) and was effectively flat on the fine mesh (83200 to 83282). Reverted the runtime change, kept outputs/profiling/ph10_same_session_ab_1m.json and outputs/profiling/perf_candidate_ph10_verify.json as evidence, and paused the card instead of landing a net-worse optimization.","x":1320,"y":4760,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"1ccaf62d","type":"text","text":"## PFL-01 Define fused backend contract and batch semantics\nDefine the canonical fused-backend scope against the conservative realtime benchmark. Make batch_size an explicit microstep-count parameter independent of servo_interval, define when the modular path remains the reference fallback, and freeze the parity requirements the fused backend must satisfy before it can replace the modular benchmark path.","x":700,"y":80,"width":420,"height":280,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"5c9e3e34","type":"text","text":"## PFL-02 Create hot-path state bundle and EDMState adapters\nBuild a Numba-compatible hot-path state representation separate from EDMState. Pack the scalar microstep state needed by the fused backend into fixed NumPy buffers with named index constants, encode optional values such as spark location and ionized-channel state with NaN sentinels, and add adapters that load from and store back to the public EDMState API without changing external behavior.","x":700,"y":860,"width":420,"height":340,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"16e0c2c2","type":"text","text":"## PFL-03 Define deterministic RNG pools for batched execution\nSpecify how the fused backend consumes randomness without calling Python inside the compiled loop. Pre-generate per-batch random pools from env.np_random, define a stable cursor/layout for ignition, short-circuit, and crater-sampling draws, and add same-seed rules so modular and fused runs can be compared reproducibly.","x":700,"y":1640,"width":420,"height":320,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"92fe9efd","type":"text","text":"## PFL-04 Prototype batched fused-loop scaffold\nAdd an optional fused backend flag and a compiled execution shell that advances an explicit batch of microsteps per Python call. The scaffold should own batch-size handling, action cadence, time advancement, RNG cursor progression, early-exit conditions, and modular fallback plumbing before it absorbs the full per-step physics.","x":700,"y":2420,"width":420,"height":280,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"9f9ae8f4","type":"text","text":"## PFL-05 Fuse full per-microstep physics into the batched backend\nMove the full microstep feedback path into the compiled backend so the fused loop remains fidelity-safe instead of becoming a benchmark-only approximation. Reuse the existing wire and ignition compiled helpers, then integrate dielectric state evolution, crater/material removal, mechanics motion, and termination-relevant updates in the same per-step order as the modular path. This card absorbs the intent of PH-14, PH-15, and PH-16 once proven.","x":700,"y":3200,"width":420,"height":340,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"7b422dd2","type":"text","text":"## PFL-06 Validate fused-vs-modular parity and promote the backend\nAdd same-seed fused-versus-modular comparison tests, verification-harness support, and dashboard reporting for the new backend. Only after parity passes should the profiler and benchmark workflow treat the fused path as the primary realtime candidate, while the modular path remains available as the reference fallback for debugging and experimentation.","x":700,"y":3980,"width":420,"height":320,"color":"6"}
	],
